// `toChar(?p)`: ask the model for exactly one character.
//
// A converter called on a whole dereference shapes the reply rather than
// converting it afterwards. That matters: if it were an ordinary call, the
// model would generate freely and the conversion would then fail on a whole
// sentence. `char(?p)` is a type check instead, and refuses the reply, which
// is a str.

prompt p = "Reply with a single letter."
let c = toChar(?p)
print(c)
print(c == "a")
